faqs:
  - q: "How is 1% processing even possible?"
    a: "We are not a standalone payment processor trying to maximize per-transaction revenue. Payment processing is one component of a complete business system that includes websites, CRM, automation, and AI. By bundling services, we can offer processing rates that traditional standalone processors cannot match. We make money on the platform, not the processing fees."
  - q: "What types of payments can I accept?"
    a: "All major credit cards (Visa, Mastercard, Amex, Discover), debit cards, ACH bank transfers, and digital wallets (Apple Pay, Google Pay). You can accept payments in person, online through your website, via invoice, or through text-to-pay links sent directly to customers."
  - q: "Is this PCI compliant and secure?"
    a: "Yes. All payment processing is fully PCI DSS Level 1 compliant — the highest level of security certification. Card data is tokenized and encrypted end-to-end. We never store raw card numbers on any server. Your customers' financial data is protected with the same security standards used by major banks."
  - q: "How fast do I get my money?"
    a: "Standard deposits arrive in your bank account within 1-2 business days. We do not hold funds or impose rolling reserves like some processors do for small businesses. Your money is your money, and you get it quickly."
  - q: "Are there any hidden fees or contracts?"
    a: "No hidden fees, no setup fees, no monthly minimums, no PCI compliance fees, no statement fees, no batch fees. The rate is 1% per transaction. Period. There are no long-term contracts — you can leave at any time with no cancellation penalties."
